# Text is checked out with LF on every system, Windows too, whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says: a test comparing a golden file byte for byte passes
# in a developer's checkout as on CI (docs/design/windows.md, decision 8).
* text=auto eol=lf
# Each release's fixture set (crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/): the files
# its own binaries wrote, held byte for byte -- never a line ending turned,
# never a diff shown. Its statements and answers are text, LF everywhere.
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/*.fennec binary
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/*.sync binary
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/*.sealed binary
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/archive/** binary
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/archive-plain/** binary
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/node-archive/** binary
crates/fennec-core/tests/compat/*/*.fennec~ binary
# The font's licence holds CRLF as its authors wrote it, kept as it is.
site/fonts/OFL-IBMPlexMono.txt -text
# Files 0.2.0 sealed, opened byte for byte: no line ending is theirs.
crates/fennec-http/tests/sealed-v1/** binary
